# URLs the links workflow does not check, each with the reason it cannot
# be checked rather than the reason it is inconvenient. Anything merely
# slow or occasionally throttled belongs in that workflow's --max-retries
# and --accept, not here.
#
# One entry, and it took a wrong one to arrive at it. The list first held
# eprint.iacr.org, on the assumption that a 403 there meant a bot filter a
# browser would pass; measured, that host answers the .pdf path with
# Cloudflare's "Just a moment..." challenge and 403 to every HTTP client,
# browser user-agent or not, while the landing page without .pdf is 200.
# So it was not unverifiable, it was the wrong URL: the citations now name
# eprint.iacr.org/<year>/<id>, which is the canonical form anyway, and
# need no exception.

# 403 from a GitHub runner and 200 from a developer machine, serving a
# 524 KB PDF: Cloudflare judging the caller's address, not the URL. There
# is no alternative form of this one -- a CHES 2006 presentation, cited by
# ec/curve_group_2.py -- so it is excluded, on the workflow's own evidence
# rather than on an assumption about it.
https://iacr\.org/workshops/.*
